{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "בן זקנים", :translit "ben zekunim", :gloss "son of elders"} {:he "זקנים", :translit "zekunim", :gloss "elders"} {:he "שהם שם ועבר", :translit "shehem shem va'eiver", :gloss "who are Shem and Eber"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Plene spelling would be זקנים with vav; defective spelling signals hidden transmission from Shem and Eber."}], :frame {:text "The midrashic tradition reads 'ben zekunim' as 'son of elders' in the sense of wisdom transmitted from elder sages. Abraham lived 175 years (Genesis 25:7) and Jacob studied in the academy of Shem and Eber before fleeing to Laban (Genesis Rabbah 68:2, 63:10). Jacob in turn transmitted this accumulated wisdom to Joseph.", :sources ["Genesis 25:7" "Genesis Rabbah 68:2" "Genesis Rabbah 63:10"]}} {:quotes [{:he "בן זקנים הוא לו", :translit "ben zekunim hu lo", :gloss "son of elders, he is to him"} {:he "ואהיה אצלו אמון ואהיה שעשועים", :translit "va'ehyeh etzlo amon va'ehyeh sha'ashu'im", :gloss "and I was beside Him as amon, and I was [His] delights"} {:he "סתרי תורה", :translit "sitrei torah", :gloss "secrets of Torah"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :sofei-tevot, :phrase "בן זקנים הוא לו", :spells "אמון"} {:kind :other, :note "The word אמון from Proverbs 8:30 is read as an allusion to סתרי תורה, secrets of Torah."}], :frame {:text "Proverbs 8 describes Wisdom speaking of being beside God as אמון (Proverbs 8:30). The word אמון is read as referring to hidden or secret aspects of Torah wisdom, linking the transmission from Jacob to Joseph with the esoteric dimension of Torah described in Proverbs 8.", :sources ["Proverbs 8:30"]}} {:quotes [{:he "זקנים", :translit "zekunim", :gloss "elders"} {:he "ר\"ז", :translit "raz", :gloss "secret"} {:he "רזי תורה", :translit "razei torah", :gloss "secrets of Torah"} {:he "זר", :translit "zar", :gloss "stranger / wreath"} {:he "עטרת זקנים בני בנים", :translit "ateret zekunim bnei vanim", :gloss "the crown of elders is grandchildren"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "זקנים", :b "ר\"ז"} {:kind :gematria, :a "זקנים", :b "זר"}], :frame {:text "Proverbs 17:6 states 'עטרת זקנים בני בנים' — the crown of elders is grandchildren. Jacob's special relationship with Joseph's children, Ephraim and Menashe, is expressed in his blessing of them in Genesis 48:9. The gematria linking זקנים to ר\"ז reinforces the reading that Jacob transmitted רזי תורה, the secrets of Torah, to Joseph.", :sources ["Proverbs 17:6" "Genesis 48:9"]}} {:quotes [{:he "זקנים", :translit "zekunim", :gloss "elders"} {:he "זרעים", :translit "zera'im", :gloss "Seeds"} {:he "קדשים", :translit "kodashim", :gloss "Sanctified"} {:he "נשים", :translit "nashim", :gloss "Women"} {:he "ישועות", :translit "yeshu'ot", :gloss "Salvations"} {:he "מועד", :translit "mo'ed", :gloss "Appointed Times"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :notarikon, :word "זקנים", :expansion ["זרעים" "קדשים" "נשים" "ישועות" "מועד"]}], :frame nil} {:quotes [{:he "פסים", :translit "pasim", :gloss "pasim (stripes/ornaments)"} {:he "פוטיפר", :translit "potiphar", :gloss "Potiphar"} {:he "סוחרים", :translit "socharim", :gloss "merchants"} {:he "ישמעאלים", :translit "yishma'elim", :gloss "Ishmaelites"} {:he "מדינים", :translit "medanim", :gloss "Medanites"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :notarikon, :word "פסים", :expansion ["פוטיפר" "סוחרים" "ישמעאלים" "מדינים"]}], :frame {:text "Genesis 37 narrates that Joseph was sold to a caravan of Ishmaelites (Genesis 37:28), and the text identifies the traders also as Medanites (Genesis 37:36). Potiphar, the Egyptian officer who purchased Joseph, is named in Genesis 39:1. The midrashic tradition traces the full chain of parties involved in Joseph's descent to Egypt from the sale initiated by the ketonet passim.", :sources ["Genesis 37:28" "Genesis 37:36" "Genesis 39:1"]}} {:quotes [{:he "פסים", :translit "pasim", :gloss "pasim"} {:he "קץ", :translit "ketz", :gloss "end"} {:he "סי\"ם", :translit "samekh yod mem", :gloss "samekh-yod-mem (=110)"} {:he "פסו תמו", :translit "pasu temu", :gloss "they ceased, they were finished"} {:he "פיוסים", :translit "piyusim", :gloss "reconciliations"} {:he "פס יד לו", :translit "pas yad lo", :gloss "the span of his hand"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "פסים", :b "קץ"} {:kind :other, :note "He states פסים also equals סי\"ם numerically, from which he derives that Joseph would rule פ' years and that סי\"ם equals the total count of Joseph's years."} {:kind :gematria, :a "פסים", :b "פס יד לו"} {:kind :other, :note "He links פסים to פסו תמו (Psalms 12:2) and to לשון פיוסים (a wordplay on reconciliation)."}], :frame {:text "Joseph lived 110 years (Genesis 50:22) and ruled in Egypt from age 30 (Genesis 41:46), producing 80 years of rule. Genesis 15:13 foretells that Abraham's descendants will be enslaved and oppressed for 400 years. The phrase פסו תמו appears in Psalms 12:2. Genesis 50:24 has Joseph tell his brothers 'I am dying,' and the midrashic tradition notes that Joseph died before all his brothers.", :sources ["Genesis 50:22" "Genesis 41:46" "Genesis 15:13" "Psalms 12:2" "Genesis 50:24"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ועשה לו כתונת פסים", :translit "va'asah lo ketonet pasim", :gloss "and he made him a ketonet pasim"} {:he "משקל שני סלעים מילת", :translit "mishkal shnei sela'im milet", :gloss "weight of two selas of silk"} {:he "שני סלעים מילת", :translit "shnei sela'im milet", :gloss "two selas of silk"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "כתונת פסים", :b "משקל שני סלעים מילת"}], :frame {:text "Shabbat 10b states that Jacob's addition of two selas' worth of fine material in the ketonet passim beyond what he gave the other brothers caused jealousy that led to the sale of Joseph and the subsequent descent of the Israelites to Egypt. The Ba'al HaTurim cites this directly as the rabbinic tradition behind his gematria.", :sources ["Shabbat 10b"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Plene spelling would be זקנים with vav; defective spelling signals hidden transmission from Shem and Eber.", :by :sel